title HUNK5 — a marketplace product page is seen on the canvas
prompt Continue the loop: next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates
think HUNK4 landed and sent (the sprite index). The design round named HUNK5 as horizon intent: a product page painted through HUNK2's Skate down-map. That is the next agent-doable crux — high-Lindy (how a catalog entry is seen), no gate, pure composition.
think The building blocks are both proven: HUNK4's sprite.render returns a product's window as a qoi.Pixmap; HUNK2's image_skate.down_map paints a Pixmap into a Skate grid reading fg_index per cell. HUNK5 is exactly render then down_map, so I compose their public API rather than re-invent either.
think Home: brushstroke/ (where the down-map and Grid live). Symlinked image/sprite.rye and image/photos.rye into brushstroke/ (qoi + tally_copy already symlinked there), mirroring how pond/apps composes across modules.
think The crux the witness must prove: the page derives from exactly the window the index pins, so it can never show a product the catalog does not name. Chose a two-tone sheet (red left, blue right) so a left-window product paints slot 3 and a right-window product paints slot 5 — an unambiguous spatial page, distinct per product.
obs Proven on metal: red-part → slot 3, blue-part → slot 5, pages differ; the page equals a direct down_map(render(product)) cell for cell (no drift); 256 lit pixels on a real canvas; unknown product refuses UnknownProduct through the composition before any paint.
obs Two build catches, both mechanical: rasterize takes a []u8 canvas (stride = width*4), not []u32 — matched HUNK2's own selftest; and the witness grep broke on an apostrophe in "window's" inside the GREEN print line (single-quoted shell string), fixed by dropping the apostrophe. GREEN after. tame_style_check exit 0, width exit 0; HUNK4 index re-run GREEN beneath.
obs Additive and reuse-only — no change to sprite.rye, photos.rye, qoi.rye, or image_skate.rye; the page composes their public API. No breach, so no cairn. No network, key, or funds — hosting a real sheet stays custody gates #2/#3.
loom witness=hunk_sprite_page_witness green=1 products=2 red_slot=3 blue_slot=5 lit_pixels=256
file brushstroke/sprite_page.rye HUNK5 — paint_product joins HUNK4's window and HUNK2's down-map into a seen product page
file tools/hunk_sprite_page_witness.rish binds the HUNK5 crux GREEN on metal; re-runs HUNK4 index beneath
file brushstroke/sprite.rye symlink to image/sprite.rye so brushstroke can compose the index
file brushstroke/photos.rye symlink to image/photos.rye — sprite's crop dependency present in brushstroke
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md folds the HUNK5 landing onto the latest-lap line; git nib refreshed same commit
recommend keep-going next agent-doable crux is HUNK6 (the sheet as a content-addressed Tablecloth artifact, a tampered sheet refusing before a product renders) or HUNK7 (a sprite-catalog manifest that travels); served/hardware rounds stay custody gates
